From: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: (ultra45_env) convert to hwmon_device_register_with_info

The driver registered an empty hwmon device and put its readings as
non-standard attributes (cpu0_temp, fan0_speed, ...) on the platform
device, so libsensors only showed the fanN_fault entries as N/A.

Use the hwmon info API with standard attributes:
 - temp1..9_input/label for the nine temperatures
 - fan1..6_input/fault/label for the CPU0, CPU1 and SYS0..SYS3 fans,
   adding the previously unexported SYS3 tach (indirect register 5)
 - fan7_fault/label for the PSU fan, which only has a status bit
Fan names and status bit order follow the obdiag env-monitor test.

The status register flags and firmware version have no hwmon
equivalent and are kept as a small extra group on the hwmon device:
status_fault, status_busy, status_stale, status_tgood,
firmware_version.

The fan speed write is dropped: it stored a computed period into the
tach register, and neither OBP nor obdiag ever writes the PIC fan
registers, the PIC controls the fans on its own.

Also fix the temperature decoding: the values use offset 64 encoding,
the s8 cast turned readings of 64 C and above negative. A raw 0
(absent sensor, e.g. CPU1 on single CPU systems) now returns -ENODATA
instead of -64 C. Resources are devm managed.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
